.TH "EPX\-SHIPPING" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-shipping \- read and change shipping zones, methods and groups, and calculate shipping fees
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping [flags]
epx shipping [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes a site\(aqs shipping configuration, calculates its shipping fees and finds the sites that ship to a postal code. Every command but find\-sites requires \fB\-\-site\fR; for an unknown site, the lists show nothing and the quotes fail.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx shipping customers"
Read and change which shipping group each customer belongs to.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping customers [flags]
epx shipping customers [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads and changes which shipping group each customer of a site belongs to.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.SS "epx shipping customers create"
Assign a customer to a shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping customers create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Assigns a customer to a shipping group of the site \fB\-\-site\fR names: the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR names the customer id and the group\(aqs, as in \fB{"customerId": "C001", "groupId": "vip"}\fR. A customer that belongs to a group already is a conflict (exit 5): change its group with update. Emporix checks neither the customer nor the group: unknown ids are assigned too.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx shipping customers delete"
Remove a customer from its shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping customers delete CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Removes the customer CUSTOMER (the customer id) from its shipping group on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names. Emporix answers a CUSTOMER without a shipping group, or an unknown one, as one that it removed (204 No Content).
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type CUSTOMER at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx shipping customers get"
Show one customer\(aqs shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping customers get CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads which shipping group each customer of a site belongs to. CUSTOMER is the customer id. Emporix answers a customer without a shipping group with an empty response, so get reports it as not found.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, GROUP.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.SS "epx shipping customers list"
List the shipping groups of customers of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping customers list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads which shipping group each customer of a site belongs to. CUSTOMER is the customer id. Emporix answers a customer without a shipping group with an empty response, so get reports it as not found.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, GROUP.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx shipping customers update"
Change the shipping group of a customer.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping customers update CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Assigns the customer CUSTOMER (the customer id) to the shipping group that the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR names, as create takes it, in place of the group it belongs to on the site \fB\-\-site\fR names; a customerId in the JSON is ignored. Emporix answers a customer without a shipping group with 409 Conflict (exit 5): the customer has no shipping group on the site: assign it one with \fBepx shipping customers create\fR.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx shipping find\-sites"
List the sites that ship to a postal code.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping find\-sites [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Lists the sites with a shipping zone that ships to a postal code: ZONES lists the zones that Emporix returns with each site, and METHODS their shipping methods (\fB\-o json\fR adds the zones\(aq destinations and fees). Emporix matched no site without \fB\-\-country\fR on the tenant tested.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among SITE, ZONES, METHODS.
.TP
\fB\-\-country <COUNTRY>\fR
The COUNTRY to ship to, a country code such as DE.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-postal\-code <POSTAL_CODE>\fR
The POSTAL_CODE to ship to (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx shipping groups"
Read and change shipping groups.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping groups [flags]
epx shipping groups [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads and changes the shipping groups of a site, which limit shipping fees to the customers assigned to them (\fBepx shipping customers\fR).
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.SS "epx shipping groups create"
Create a shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping groups create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a shipping group of the site \fB\-\-site\fR names from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its id and description, as in \fB{"id": "vip", "description": {"en": "Free shipping"}}\fR. A fee of a shipping method applies to the customers of a group (\fBepx shipping customers create\fR) when it names the group as its shippingGroupId. Emporix answers with the group\(aqs id; a group with that id exists already: a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Netherlands", "nl": "Nederland"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent without a Content\-Language header (\fB\-\-content\-language\fR *, the default), or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, sent with that Content\-Language, e.g. \fB"Netherlands"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations, sent without Content\-Language. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx shipping groups delete"
Delete a shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping groups delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the shipping group ID of the site \fB\-\-site\fR names. Fees of shipping methods that name it as their shippingGroupId stay and still name it, and customers assigned to it stay assigned to it (\fBepx shipping customers\fR). Emporix answers an unknown ID as one that it deleted (204 No Content).
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx shipping groups get"
Show one shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping groups get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the shipping groups of a site, which limit shipping fees to the customers assigned to them (\fBepx shipping customers\fR). Emporix answers an unknown group with 409 Conflict, so get fails with exit code 1.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, DESCRIPTION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.SS "epx shipping groups list"
List the shipping groups of a site.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping groups list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the shipping groups of a site, which limit shipping fees to the customers assigned to them (\fBepx shipping customers\fR). Emporix answers an unknown group with 409 Conflict, so get fails with exit code 1.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
