.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, DESCRIPTION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx shipping groups update"
Replace a shipping group.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping groups update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the shipping group ID of the site \fB\-\-site\fR names with the group in \fB\-\-file\fR, as create takes it. Emporix answers an unknown ID with 409 Conflict (exit 5): the site has no shipping group with this ID: \fBepx shipping groups list \-\-site S\fR lists them.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Netherlands", "nl": "Nederland"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent without a Content\-Language header (\fB\-\-content\-language\fR *, the default), or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, sent with that Content\-Language, e.g. \fB"Netherlands"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations, sent without Content\-Language. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx shipping quote"
Calculate the shipping fee of each method to a destination.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping quote [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Calculates what each shipping method of a site\(aqs zones that ship to a destination costs for a cart total: one row per method, with its zone, its FEE and its shipping TAX CODE. With \fB\-\-customer\fR, the fees of the customer\(aqs shipping group apply (\fBepx shipping customers\fR). Emporix answers a destination or cart total that no method serves, or an unknown site, with 400 Bad Request (exit 1).
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-cart\-total <AMOUNT CURRENCY>\fR
The cart\(aqs total as AMOUNT CURRENCY, e.g. \fB"100 EUR"\fR (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ZONE, METHOD, NAME, FEE, TAX CODE.
.TP
\fB\-\-country <COUNTRY>\fR
The destination COUNTRY, a country code such as DE (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-customer <CUSTOMER>\fR
The CUSTOMER id, whose shipping group\(aqs fees apply.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-postal\-code <POSTAL_CODE>\fR
The destination POSTAL_CODE (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.SS "epx shipping quote\-minimum"
Calculate the lowest shipping fee to a destination.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping quote\-minimum [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Calculates the lowest shipping fee of a site to a destination for a cart total, as a cart shows it before a delivery window is chosen. TAX CODE is the method\(aqs shipping tax code. Emporix answers a destination or cart total that no method serves, or an unknown site, with 400 Bad Request (exit 1).
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-cart\-total <AMOUNT CURRENCY>\fR
The cart\(aqs total as AMOUNT CURRENCY, e.g. \fB"100 EUR"\fR (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among FEE, TAX CODE.
.TP
\fB\-\-country <COUNTRY>\fR
The destination COUNTRY, a country code such as DE (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-customer <CUSTOMER>\fR
The CUSTOMER id, whose shipping group\(aqs fees apply.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-postal\-code <POSTAL_CODE>\fR
The destination POSTAL_CODE (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.SS "epx shipping quote\-slot"
Calculate the shipping fee of a delivery time slot.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping quote\-slot [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Calculates the shipping fee of a delivery time slot for a cart total: \fB\-\-delivery\-time\fR and \fB\-\-slot\fR are the IDs that \fBepx delivery\-times list\fR and \fBepx delivery\-times slots list\fR show. The destination is optional; \fB\-\-country\fR and \fB\-\-postal\-code\fR go together. An unknown delivery time is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-cart\-total <AMOUNT CURRENCY>\fR
The cart\(aqs total as AMOUNT CURRENCY, e.g. \fB"100 EUR"\fR (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among FEE, TAX CODE.
.TP
\fB\-\-country <COUNTRY>\fR
The destination COUNTRY, a country code such as DE.
.TP
\fB\-\-customer <CUSTOMER>\fR
The CUSTOMER id, whose shipping group\(aqs fees apply.
.TP
\fB\-\-delivery\-time <ID>\fR
The delivery time\(aqs ID (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-postal\-code <POSTAL_CODE>\fR
The destination POSTAL_CODE.
.TP
\fB\-\-site <site>\fR
Site code, e.g. main (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-slot <ID>\fR
The ID of the delivery time\(aqs slot (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.SS "epx shipping zones"
Read and change shipping zones and their methods.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping zones [flags]
epx shipping zones [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads and changes the shipping zones of a site and the shipping methods of a zone.
.PP
Its reads need no OAuth scope. Its writes require the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.SS "epx shipping zones create"
Create a shipping zone.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shipping zones create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a shipping zone of the site \fB\-\-site\fR names from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its id, name, shipTo (the countries it ships to, each with a postal code, or a prefix followed by *, where it ships to some only) and whether it is the site\(aqs default zone, as in \fB{"id": "nl", "name": {"en": "Netherlands"}, "shipTo": [{"country": "NL"}], "default": true}\fR. The first zone of a site becomes its default zone whatever default says. Emporix answers with the zone\(aqs id; a zone with that id exists already: a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "Netherlands", "nl": "Nederland"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, sent without a Content\-Language header (\fB\-\-content\-language\fR *, the default), or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, sent with that Content\-Language, e.g. \fB"Netherlands"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations, sent without Content\-Language. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
